& =\frac{50}{M^{\prime}} \mathrm{M}...(ii)
\end{aligned}

Equating both equations (i) and (ii), we get

\begin{aligned}
\frac{50}{M^{\prime}} & =0.7309 \\
M^{\prime} & =\frac{50}{0.7309} \\
& =68.408 \mathrm{~g} \mathrm{~mol}^{-1}
\end{aligned}

Hence, molecular weight of $A$ is $68.4 \mathrm{~g} \mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$.

